IV. Results A. Implementation and Validation
Consider the examples shown in Fig. 2, in which an MH-60 helicopter is hovering above the ship deck of a Formidable-class frigate. The ship geometry was taken from [6]. In Fig. 2a, the helicopter is hovering on top of the deck, whereas in Fig. 2b the helicopter is crossing the ship deck. In both examples, the ship and helicopter have a longitudinal velocity of 18 kts, corresponding to the cruise speed of the Formidable-class frigate. The coupled rotor and state-space free-vortex wake model is implemented in MATLAB®/Simulink using a 10 deg time step, corresponding to a dimensional time step of approximately dt 6.46e − 4 s, and four revolutions of rotor wake. The resulting NLTP system has a state vector with dimension n 2448 (20 rotor states and 2428 wake states), a control vector with dimension m 17 and an output vector
